== 5. The Ignorant

#strong[Lastly, #emph[as Satan has his] devices #emph[to destroy gracious souls, so he has his devices to destroy poor ignorant souls, and that sometimes]]

BY drawing them to choose ignorance, and to neglect, slight and#footnote[Hos 4:6. Prov 19:2.] despise the means of knowledge. Ignorance is the mother of mistake, the cause of trouble, error and terror;#footnote[Matt 22:29.] it is the highway to hell, and it makes a man both a prisoner and a slave to the devil at once. Ignorance unmans a#footnote[The ignorant have this advantage (#emph[ut mitius ardeant]): they have a cooler hell.] man; it makes a man a beast; indeed, it makes him more miserable than the beast that perishes. There are none so easily or so frequently taken in Satan’s snare as ignorant souls. They are easily drawn to dance with the devil all day, and to dream of supping with Christ at night, etc.

#strong[Now the remedies against this device of Satan are as follows.]

The first #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider solemnly that an ignorant heart is an evil heart: “Without knowledge, the mind is not good.”#footnote[Prov 19:2.]

An ignorant heart is a wicked heart; it is a heart in the dark, and no#footnote[#emph[Ignorat sane improbus omnis] \[Every wicked man is ignorant indeed\], says Aristotle. Matt 6:22.] good can come into a dark heart without passing through the understanding: “and if your eye is dark, your whole body will be full of darkness.” A leprous head and a leprous heart are inseparable companions. Ignorant hearts are so evil that they lash out on every side, and do not hold back from spitting their venom in the very face of God, as Pharaoh did when thick darkness was on him.

The second #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider that ignorance is the deformity of the soul. As blindness is the deformity of the face, so ignorance is the deformity of the soul; as the lack of bodily eyes spoils the beauty of the face, so the lack of spiritual eyes spoils the beauty of the soul. A man without knowledge is like a workman without his hands, a painter without his eyes, a traveler without his legs, a ship without sails, a bird without wings, or a body without a soul.

The third #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider solemnly that ignorance makes men the objects of God’s hatred and wrath. “Their hearts#footnote[Heb 3:10, 11. Those who do not know God’s ways must go astray; and yet they cannot wander so far as to miss hell. Isa 27:11. 2 Thess 1:8.] are always going astray, and they have not known My ways. So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’” “This is a people without understanding. Therefore their Maker has no compassion on them.” Christ has said that #emph[he will come in blazing fire, inflicting vengeance on those who do not know God.] Ignorance will end in vengeance. When you see a poor blind man here, you do not loathe him or hate him, but you pity him; oh! but soul-blindness makes you abominable in the sight of God. God has sworn that ignorant persons will never come into heaven; heaven#footnote[Hos 4:6. נדמו cut off. Rome says ignorance is the mother of devotion, but the Scripture says it is the mother of destruction.] itself would be a hell to ignorant souls. “My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge. Because you have rejected knowledge, I will also reject you.”

Chilo, one of the seven sages, being asked what God had done, answered, “He has exalted humble men and brought down proud, ignorant fools.”

The fourth #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider that ignorance is a sin that leads to all sins. All sins are in ignorance as in their seed: “You#super[+] are mistaken#footnote[Matt 22:29.] because you#super[+] do not know the Scriptures.” It drives men to hate and persecute the saints: “They will hate you#super[+] and put you#super[+]#footnote[John 16:2, 3.] out of the synagogues. In fact, a time is coming when anyone who kills you#super[+] will think#footnote[Aristotle makes ignorance the mother of all the misrule in the world. 1 Tim 1:13.] he is offering a service to God. They will do these things because they have not known the Father or Me.” Paul lays all his cruelties to Christians at the door of his ignorance: “I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and a violent man; yet because I had acted in ignorance … I was shown mercy.” It was ignorance that drove the Jews to crucify Christ. “Father, forgive them,” says Christ of his murderers, “for they do not know#footnote[1 Cor 2:8.] what they are doing.” “For if the rulers of this age had understood it, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.” Sin at first was the cause of ignorance, but now ignorance is the cause of all sin. “Cursing#footnote[They did as Oedipus did, who killed his father Laius, king of Thebes, and thought he was killing his enemy.] and lying, murder and stealing, and adultery are rampant,” says the prophet, because there is no knowledge of God in the land. There are none so frequent and so impudent in the ways of sin as ignorant souls. They do not care or heed what they do, or what they say against God, Christ, heaven, holiness and their own souls: “Our tongues#footnote[Hos 4:1, 2. Ps 73:8, 9.] are our own; who will be master over us?” “They mock and speak with malice; with arrogance they threaten oppression. They set their mouths against the heavens, and their tongues strut across the earth.” “Have all the#footnote[Ps 14:4.] workers of iniquity no knowledge? They devour my people like bread; they refuse to call upon the #smallcaps[Lord].”
